.TH AGENT-HOOK-PROMPT-SUBMIT 1 "2026-10-13" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-prompt-submit \- handle prompt-time agent context refresh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-prompt-submit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-prompt-submit
reads a prompt-submit hook JSON payload from standard input and delegates
memory-intent reminders and prompt-time context refresh policy to
.BR "hm hook prompt-submit" .
It then resets once-per-prompt AgentGuard state used by edit and command
guidance. Unless an extension blocks the prompt, a prompt with text also marks
the agent's tmux pane busy with
.BR "term-pane-mark set busy" ,
when that command is installed. It changes the mark only while the agent
process that runs the hook is the pane terminal's foreground program, so an
agent it launches, which inherits the pane but not its terminal, can neither
set nor clear it. A Codex session without a transcript is not tracked: that
covers Codex's in-process background agents (memory consolidation, task
titles), and also a
.B codex exec \-\-ephemeral
run directly in a pane;
.BR agent-hook-stop (1)
clears the mark when the turn ends.
.PP
On Claude Code, Codex, and Muse the hook asks Hive Memory to track delivery:
it passes the host's context lifetime and size limit, minus room for context
that earlier pushed a response over the limit after Hive Memory's block.
Hive Memory counts what it emits within that limit as delivered. When the
host would not show it after all, a context reset is left pending so the next
prompt re-sends. Memory context that would push the response over the limit
is removed, and the overflowing context after it is reserved from then on. A
failed Hive Memory call, a response the hook cannot write, or a prompt it
blocks also leave the reset pending, except a blocked Muse prompt, whose
memory context never counts as delivered. The pending reset is cleared once
a tracked response re-sends memory context (even only a header) under it.
With less than 2 KB left, or after three overflows since the last compaction,
clear, or resume, the prompt runs untracked, as without tracking.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_HOOKS
Set to
.B 0
to disable Hive Memory hook integration.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_DELIVERY
Set to
.BR 0 ,
.BR false ,
.BR no ,
or
.B off
to keep every runtime on untracked Hive Memory hooks.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_CONTEXT_RESERVE
Minimum bytes of the host limit to keep free for context added after Hive
Memory (default 0). The hook otherwise reserves the context that last pushed
a response over the limit (capped at half the limit unless two overflows were
consecutive) until the next compaction, clear, or resume, or a Muse
project-change block.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Prompt handling completed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hm (1),
.BR agent-hook-compact (1),
.BR agent-hook-session-start (1),
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
